What is Gravimetric Feeder (Loss-in-Weight)?
Gravimetric feeders are precision instruments designed to deliver a controlled mass flow of materials in industrial processes. Unlike volumetric feeders that measure by volume, these systems operate by continuously weighing material loss from a hopper and adjusting the feed rate accordingly. The technology excels in handling diverse materials - from free-flowing powders to cohesive bulk solids - while maintaining high accuracy typically within ±0.25%.

